{
 "kind": "item",
 "name": "Frame-and-panel door",
 "category": "component",
 "_about": "a cupboard's door as a joiner makes it: two stiles and two rails round a thinner panel set back in them; its face at z 0 looking +z (`anchor` 1, the default; 0: its back at z 0 and its face at t, as modern/components/slab-door stands), `w` by `h`; a knob by its opening edge (side -1 left, 1 right; `knob` 0: none -- the modern slab-door's shaker front puts its own pull); the panel is role `panel` (its own `wood` unless the user maps it: a darker or other sunk panel) -- `swing` 1: HINGED at the edge away from its knob (side), opening out toward +z with the item's `open`",
